s://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5791,"closed_issues":0,"state":"open","created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-21T22:40:26Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-06-10T18:23:17Z","updated_at":"2026-07-01T21:55:05Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/120161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120161","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120161.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120161.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Related to [#14991](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14991)\r\n- Related to [#14993](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/14993)\r\n\r\nThis PR improves deadzone state handling and flick detection in VirtualJoystick.\r\n\r\nChanges included:\r\n\r\n- Added `get_is_in_deadzone()`.\r\n- Added `deadzone_entered` signal.\r\n- Added `deadzone_exited` signal.\r\n- Updated `flicked` and `flick_canceled` behavior.\r\n\r\n`flicked` is now emitted only when the pointer leaves the deadzone once and does not re-enter it before release.\r\n\r\n`flick_canceled` is emitted once when a potential flick becomes invalid by re-entering the deadzone before release.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nThe implementation is small and is provided to demonstrate a possible solution for the discussions in #14991 and #14993.\r\n\r\nI understand that changing the behavior of documented signals during the release candidate stage may not be desirable due to API stability concerns. This PR is mainly intended to make the proposed changes easier to evaluate by providing a working implementation.\r\n\r\nThis PR only implements one of the approaches discussed in #14993. Additional discussion may be needed regarding whether flick detection should also consider factors such as:\r\n\r\n- A configurable time limit.\r\n- Pointer movement speed. (I think a time limit should be enough)\r\n\r\nTest videos are attached for all VirtualJoystick modes:\r\n\r\n1. Fixed\r\n2. Dynamic\r\n3. Following\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb867396-eb3f-4d9b-a8b5-48143a60f132\r\n\r\n","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120161/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120161/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}